[0.746, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[3J\u001b[1;38;2;139;123;255m  ____                  _\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[1;38;2;117;115;233m / ___|  ___  _ __ ___ | |    ___  __ _ _ __ _ __\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[1;38;2;94;106;210m \\___ \\ / _ \\| '__/ _ \\| |   / _ \\/ _` | '__| '_ \\\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[1;38;2;75;148;229m  ___) | (_) | | | (_) | |__|  __/ (_| | |  | | | |\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[1;38;2;56;189;248m |____/ \\___/|_|  \\___/|_____\\___|\\__,_|_|  |_| |_|\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\nWelcome to Sorolearn: small exercises that teach you to write\r\r\nSoroban smart contracts on Stellar.\r\r\n\r\r\nHow it works:\r\r\n  1. Open the exercise shown below in your editor.\r\r\n  2. Make it compile and make its tests pass.\r\r\n  3. Save. Sorolearn re-runs the tests automatically.\r\r\n  4. When it passes, press `n` for the next exercise.\r\r\n\r\r\nEach topic folder has a README.md with background reading.\r\r\nStuck? Press `h` for a hint.\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[2mPress any key to start...\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
