[3.535, "o", "\r\r\n\u001b[1mHint for\u001b[0m \u001b[36mtransactions2\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n- Hash a `TransactionSignaturePayload`, not the bare transaction:\r\r\n    let payload = TransactionSignaturePayload {\r\r\n        network_id: Hash(network_id(passphrase)),\r\r\n        tagged_transaction: TransactionSignaturePayloadTaggedTransaction::Tx(tx.clone()),\r\r\n    };\r\r\n  then sha256 its XDR (`payload.to_xdr(Limits::none())`).\r\r\n- The hint is the *last* 4 bytes of the public key: `public_key[28..]`.\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1mh\u001b[0m:hint  \u001b[1ml\u001b[0m:list  \u001b[1mr\u001b[0m:rerun  \u001b[1mq\u001b[0m:quit   \u001b[2m(press a key)\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[5.774, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[3J\u001b[1mChecking\u001b[0m \u001b[36mexercises/12_stellar_transactions/transactions2.rs\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m(compiling... the first build of the Soroban SDK can take a minute)\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[1.213, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[3J\u001b[32m✓ Exercise transactions2 passed!\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\nRead through the code once more: the comments explain why it works.\r\r\n\u001b[2mSolution for comparison: solutions/12_stellar_transactions/transactions2.rs\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
