[3.054, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[3J🎉 You finished every Sorolearn exercise!\r\r\n\r\r\nYou can write, test and *review* Soroban contracts (storage, auth, errors,\r\r\nevents, tokens, cross-contract calls, time, and the security bugs AI-written\r\r\ncontracts actually ship with), and you know the Stellar network underneath\r\r\nthem: accounts, keys, multisig, transactions, signatures and assets.\r\r\n\r\r\nGraduate on-chain: run `sorolearn graduate`. It deploys your quiz1 poll to\r\r\nStellar testnet, where the Sorolearn registry contract examines it and\r\r\nrecords you as a graduate. See exercises/15_testnet/README.md.\r\r\n\r\r\nWhere to go next:\r\r\n  - Install the Stellar CLI and deploy a contract to testnet:\r\r\n    https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/smart-contracts/getting-started\r\r\n  - Read real-world examples: https://github.com/stellar/soroban-examples\r\r\n  - Build something and ship it!\r\r\n"]
